            <ArticleTitle>Multiple-vessel coronary revascularization with combined in situ and free sequential internal mammary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>301-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bilateral internal mammary arteries were used sequentially (one as an in situ graft to provide inflow and the other as a free graft to provide outflow) in a patient with multiple-vessel coronary artery disease requiring revascularization without an autologous venous conduit available.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
